WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.060
My name is Vaati.

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.040
And welcome to Dark Souls 2.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.200
So I'm not the kind of person
or not the kind of channel

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.060
to do things in half-measures.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:14.000
My videos require a lot of editing
and let's plays rarely require much.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.440
So in this series I'm going to make it different.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.920
I'm gonna keep it fast-paced.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.280
Maybe even introduce a new theme
to every episode, you know...

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.760
The theme of this episode is:
how to get the best possible start.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.180
So I ask you guys,
my subscribers:

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.680
to join me in adventuring
through Drangleic.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.400
There's a lot to see and we're going to be discovering this entire game,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.140
one video at a time in 2014.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.820
Things Betwixt

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.160
A huge part of this game
is curing the curse of undeath.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.400
Our character travels to
this old decrepit castle,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.240
but upon arriving he realizes that it has another side to it.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:53.180
And further on in the cinematic
he actually gets drawn into this vortex,

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.780
and I say drawn because,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.720
he's not just drawn
by some need to cure the curse.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.400
It seems like he's literally forced
into this hole:

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.360
his pupil explodes in Darkness
and his hand starts writhing,

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:07.580
and this just indicates to me
that he's being drawn in there.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.620
Anyway, as you progress through
you come across these dogs.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.420
And you know, this is the reason the start of Dark Souls 2 really appeals to me,

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:17.000
And it's probably
my masochistic side saying this:

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.640
but if you wait in this section too long,
these dogs start to surround you,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.240
and if you provoke them, like I've done,
then they'll chase you down,

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.220
and make you become a bit more wary of the fact
that you're wearing rags,

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.300
and that you have like
no health.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.800
They chase you towards
this warm light...

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.500
..and that's where
we're gonna go next.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.100
I actually spy this item off near this tree,

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.260
this is something you should pick up, 
because we'll find its use later in the tutorial.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.640
In regards to this cinematic:
you can skip it if you like,

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.580
but I have overlaid a lot of game-play
so it's more interesting.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.420
"Heh heh heh...
What seems to be the ruckus?

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.500
Ooh, my!
Your face.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.540
The face of the curse."

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.340
"It's an Undead.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.800
An Undead has come to play.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.760
Heh heh...

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:18.680
They all end up here,
all the ones like you.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.500
You spoke to that kind old dear,

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.680
didn't you?

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.880
Heh heh...

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.380
You're finished.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.520
You'll go Hollow.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.480
Yes, you will become one of them.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.960
Hollows prey upon men...

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.980
..feast upon their souls.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.680
This is the fate of the cursed.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.080
Heh heh heh..."

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.740
THE OLD LADIES LAUGH

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.760
So, we're not the only ones
who were drawn here.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.140
Let's find out a bit more about
where we are:

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.360
"This is a limbo.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.900
A link between Drangleic...

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.220
..and the outer world.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.480
Fair traveler...

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.920
..I know that you must have a story.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.920
Why else would you visit
such a place?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.500
This lost, decayed kingdom.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:25.520
My name is Milibeth.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.360
The old women were once Fire Keepers.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.640
I am here to look after them.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.500
It is what my mother did,

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.080
and her mother before her,

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.100
and so on.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.160
But now, the fire shows
signs of fading…

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:47.260
And the kingdom...
..is beset by Hollows.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.520
The old women are sisters.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.440
I am told there was a fourth.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.700
Long ago,
Fire Keepers were commonplace.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.860
But now they are lost,
scattered to the winds."

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.000
VAATI:
So after being made fun of for a little while,
by all these old women,

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.500
we're gonna head back outside,
into the tutorial area.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.080
If you were watching during that cinematic 
then you would have seen me

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.680
go through this hole in the bushes,
just before that bridge.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.000
And this guy, this is the reason
we picked a sorcerer:

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.720
So we could take out this guy.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.720
As soon as you see
these big enemies,

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.320
I'm sure you're all thinking:

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.240
"You know if I kill that now,
I bet I get an awesome item!"

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.200
And you do get a pretty cool item
from this guy,

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.600
he's the only Ogre in this level
that will give you an item.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.460
The item is called:
Stone Ring.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.400
What it does is:

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.520
every time you hit an enemy
it decreases their poise,

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.740
a lot more than if you
didn't have the ring on.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:47.860
So basically you'll break their poise more often
when you smash them,

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.380
and I think that's really good for weapons
that attack quickly,

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.840
although I'm not sure.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.260
So now he's gone,
we're gonna take his item.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.340
Further on is some Gold Pine Resin.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:59.580
And then we're gonna continue
with the actual tutorial,

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.820
which I won't show much of,
because it's not that interesting.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:07.260
"You must go, on a journey without rest.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.060
Well...I suppose,
if you find yourself at an impasse...

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.980
But if your will
is yet unbroken...

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.560
..then you may return here.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.500
To start again,

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.440
with a clean slate...

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:27.540
Hah hah hah..."

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.540
VAATI:
So, the journey begins:

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.920
Light this bonfire.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:36.160
Over to the right is a wagon:
behind the wagon is a torch.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:39.180
I think I should mention
how the torch mechanic works in this game:

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:43.420
every torch contributes 5 minutes of lit time
towards your counter.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.580
You can light the torch at the bonfire,

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.560
by toggling with triangle
or whatever button that is on Xbox.

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:50.060
And you can light your torch.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.820
Right now I'm like, you know,
there's so many torches in this tutorial...

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.120
I'm going to light
every single one of them,

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.320
I am going to see
if something happens.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.300
As one of our characters
is currently doing that...

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.580
..our other character
is going to check out this coffin.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.900
We'll go back to the character
who's lighting torches...

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.300
But for now,
let's see what this coffin is:

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.720
It's surrounded by these Ogres,
surely if you get in, something happens, right?

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.620
I just want you guys,
if you haven't got in the coffin:

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.820
try it, and tell me
what you noticed changes.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:21.160
Something changes.
I'm not going to tell you.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.020
First time I found this coffin,
it was like...

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.000
..in previous versions of the game
it actually floated away,

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.440
and you're just like:
"Okay, am I going to another area?"

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.160
But no, you appear in the same area.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.400
As soon as you get out: 
you're attacked 
by these two guys immediately.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.460
You don't get a chance to think,
and I think that was intentional.

00:06:36.460 --> 00:06:39.820
They know you couldn't kill them,
so they wanted you to run to it, and get in,

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:41.420
and try to figure out
what's changed.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.680
It took me like,
I got halfway through my game,

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.140
before I realized
what changed.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:47.300
And I want to know
if you guys figured it out.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.700
Go trough the tutorial:
you'll find a nest.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.080
And I think you know
what's coming...

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.580
Drop the Smooth Silky Stone
we found earlier in the level,

00:06:56.587 --> 00:06:59.107
or drop the Petrified Something
that you started with,

00:06:59.107 --> 00:07:00.600
and you'll get a reward.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.600
DYNA:
"Yah, yah, so nice, so smooth."

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.580
TILLO:
"Yah, yah, silky smooth."

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.180
So Snuggly the Crow is back,
and it looks like she has a friend.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.580
Anyway back to our Cleric,
who is currently lighting torches,

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.300
you get to the end and:

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.880
FLATLY:
nothing happens.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.280
Don't light the torches,
it's a waste of time...

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:22.180
So let's finish this tutorial
with our main character.

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:26.460
Honestly, I didn't need to light a torch
for this little cave section, but...

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.060
..you know darkness on YouTube
isn't a great thing...

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:32.560
..and any excuse to use a torch
 I just jump at in this game.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:37.740
I love the way the shadows look,
and the way the lighting looks is just incredible, especially at the start of the game.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.660
So you come out into Majula,

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.500
your eyes take a second
to adjust to the harsh light.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:47.500
And this is the hub area
that you're going to be traveling back to.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.360
There are a bunch of
important NPC's in Majula,

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:54.500
and coming back after a boss
to spend your souls and rest is a huge thing.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.840
LENIGRAST:
"Who are you?

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.740
Oh, it doesn't matter,

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.560
just help me open this door.

00:08:04.149 --> 00:08:07.589
I packed my tools in here,
seeing it was vacant...

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:12.060
..but now somebody's gone
and locked the door."

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:16.480
And that's Lenigrast; the blacksmith who can't fit
through the giant open window(!)

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:19.480
We're going to find the key for his house
a little bit later in the walkthrough.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:25.680
But for now,
we're going to talk to the woman
who is probably the most important character in Majula.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.980
EMERALD HERALD:
"Are you...the next monarch?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.580
Or...merely a pawn of fate?

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.960
Bearer of the curse...

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:45.240
I will remain by your side.
Till this frail hope shatters...

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.080
Take this with you.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:51.660
May it ease your journey.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.780
Go on, and see the King.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:59.700
He who made Drangleic
what it once was;

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.400
he who peered at
the essence of the soul:

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.620
King Vendrick.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:09.540
Bearer of the curse,
seek misery.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.120
For misery will lead you to
greater, stronger souls.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:21.160
You will never meet the King
with a soul so frail and pallid.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.020
Seek those whose names
are unutterable,

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.260
the four endowed
with immense souls.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.960
Their souls will serve
as beacons.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:40.380
Once you have found them,
return here to me.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.040
So that hope will not fade away."

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:48.020
VAATI:
"So that hope will not fade away."
God, I love that dialogue!

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:51.480
I especially love the bit
where she talks about finding the King.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:56.900
I really like when games set up the fact that you're going to be this incredible character later on,

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.460
you start off small,
but later in the game

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:02.980
you know you're going to take out someone
who is a huge problem,

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:06.380
or someone who is hugely powerful
compared to you.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.360
So now we're going to adventure through
the Forest of the Fallen Giants.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.920
And that name, and this area,
is interesting from a lore perspective.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.980
Long ago, there was a battle,
a war with the Giants.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:21.440
And whenever a Giant fell in battle:
a tree would grow from its point of death.

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.400
And that's essentially
what this entire forest is made of.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:29.080
So you can get some sort of idea
of the scale of the battle
that must have taken place.

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:32.340
And when I played through this for the first time,
and even now,

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:34.920
I thought:
"God damn, that's great game design"

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:38.260
You come up from the ladder
and you see this vista.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:40.540
And immediately
there's so much to take in:

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:43.940
There's four enemies wandering around,
that you're going to have to take out.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:46.340
There's this archer up the top,
shooting at you.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.360
And there's this little crestfallen knight,
sitting at the tree;

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:51.880
You don't know, is he hostile?
Is he going to attack me?

00:10:51.899 --> 00:10:54.620
Soon enough you figure out:
no, he's not going to attack you.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:58.280
In previous versions of the game though,
he used to be very aggressive.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:02.660
In previous versions of the game:
you actually had to skirt
around the outside of the arena

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.460
in case you got too close to him.

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:06.640
Because if you got too close,
he would attack you.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.640
But in this version,
we're going to run up this side passage,

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:11.640
and we're going
to take out the archer.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.880
And then we're going
to fight the Heide Knight.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:17.380
And the Heide Knight drops
a really, really good straight sword;

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:21.800
its imbued with Lightning,
does a good amount of damage,
has an all right move set.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:27.160
Personally I like the Longsword
-- that we're going to find in a few minutes --
a little bit better.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.420
So killing him is fairly optional,

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.420
but you know,
if you feel like fighting him:

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:32.400
go for it.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.340
He's definitely not
an easy fight,

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:37.380
and we'll go through the fight
a little bit in detail in about a minute.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.500
But right now:
let's take out this archer.

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:41.740
Just take him out...

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:44.440
..I'm good at this game,
I promise.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:45.960
See...

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:47.600
..oh, I almost fell off,
but I didn't.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.920
I'm so good(!)

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.680
So this character isn't
going to kill the Heide Knight.

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:54.760
We're going to actually get a fire Longsword,
later in the level.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.540
So this character is gonna make this jump,
get this item.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:59.680
And I'll show you
how to kill the Heide Knight.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:03.500
My hot tips for this guy
revolve around one thing:

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.080
learn his moveset!

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.760
As soon as he finishes his moves;
attack him once,

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:11.700
you'll have just enough time to roll away,
before his next one connects with you.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.000
He does have a few moves
that will surprise you,

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.920
but those are surprises,
and this is Dark Souls!

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.540
So I'm not going
to spoil them for you.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:18.840
What is this?
A walkthrough(?!)

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.260
So let's grab his sword
and continue with the walkthrough...

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.640
So we continue along up these stairs
and we take out a group of enemies.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.720
A common trend I've found in Dark Souls 2
is to take out melee enemies

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.060
while having a ranged enemy
attacking you in some way.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:35.300
Make sure you be careful of those fire bombs:
they do a fair bit of damage!

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:37.580
So after this we're going to climb this ladder,

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:40.180
we're going to go inside, 
and we're going to light a bonfire.

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:40.940
Finally!

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.960
One thing to mention about lighting bonfires
this time around is that:

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:46.980
The act of lighting a bonfire,
triggers it as a checkpoint.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:49.020
Which means you no longer have to rest there,

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:51.660
and respawn enemies,
to trigger it as a checkpoint.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.080
This is Melentia.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.480
She sells a bunch of
great consumable items:

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:57.780
5 Human Effigies, 10 Radiant Lifegems,

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.240
Throwing Knives, 
which are wonderful this time around.

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:03.640
And most importantly,
the Blacksmith's key,
which you're gonna need.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:06.960
But once we've got the blacksmith unlocked,
we need something to upgrade!

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:10.300
So we're going to get
what is probably my favorite starting weapon:

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:11.800
The fire Longsword.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.540
And it's in an interesting location.

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.000
So once you've
dropped down that ledge,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.220
It's a matter of doing some minor platforming
to make it down to the bottom,

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:20.520
while taking out
these Hollow Soldiers on the way.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.480
Interesting thing about
these Hollow Soldiers:

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.620
they were once part of the war
against the Giants,

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:25.980
but they've all Hollowed now.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:29.480
You can just see that: 
they're destined to wander around here aimlessly,

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:31.740
until they see someone's souls to take.

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:35.660
So this is a cave that turns away
a lot of new players.

00:13:35.666 --> 00:13:37.760
At this point,
you might have been playing for a while,

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:39.600
or you don't exactly feel
like dying,

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:42.300
and when you see
this cave full of fire, you're like:

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.820
"Will that burn me when I go in?"

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:47.060
You go in a bit further, there's this thing shooting fireballs, and you're like:

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:48.820
"I'm not going in there."

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.500
But it rewards
the courageous player,

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:54.320
it rewards the person
who's looking to take risks.

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:56.500
Grab this tentatively and run back.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:59.660
And you might be able to spy
this door to the left:

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:01.760
open it quickly,
in between bursts.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.080
Maybe better than I did,
and you might be lucky enough to roll inside.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:07.180
This...is the fire Longsword.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.960
And it's probably
my favorite weapon so far.

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.640
if you don't feel like using the fire Longsword
for whatever reason,

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:16.199
there are a lot of options
you can actually get from the Blacksmith,

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.400
so head back to Majula,
rest, spend your souls.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.720
And then we'll head
deeper into this castle.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:24.820
We've seen some ambushes
in previous levels,

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:27.500
but it's nothing compared
to what you're gonna see here.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.012
I think one good rule of thumb
for this level is;

00:14:30.012 --> 00:14:31.229
if an enemy looks dead:

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:34.740
It's not dead, and it's going to
try and kill you later in the level.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:37.560
So make sure you get the first hit in,
like I am.

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:40.960
Eventually we're going to make it
to a fog gate.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:44.980
And this is where you make a choice,
because this is where the path branches.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:49.720
Over to the right: we see this decrepit housing
further down lower by the wall.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:52.240
On the wall,
on the ramparts:

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.160
we see a bunch of enemies
that are actually quite tricky to take out.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.080
Especially as you get further on,
you'll see what I mean...

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:01.840
To end up that ladder is death,
let's not go there right now right now.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:05.040
Right now, we're going to see these barrels
at the far end, near a wall.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:08.360
If you see black barrels near a wall:
I think you know what to do to them...

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:10.060
..I'm gonna show you
what to do to them.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.580
This is what you do to them:

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:16.080
After you've been blown up
by 10 barrels of gunpowder...

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:17.720
..just walk it off, you know.

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:19.220
Go through this hole
in the wall you created,

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:21.280
and you'll realize:
you created a shortcut.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.960
At this point in the game,
if you climb this ladder,

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:27.560
I hope you've spent all your souls,
because you're most likely going to die.

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:31.320
Up this ladder is one of the only
bosses that comes to you,

00:15:31.328 --> 00:15:33.050
and he only comes to you once.

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:36.820
So you get one chance to take him out here, 
if you don't take him out here:

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:39.270
you can fight him later in the level,
in a designated area.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.040
If you fight him early,
do you get something special for it?

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:43.400
Well, let's see.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.740
This is the Pursuer.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:47.740
SILENCE

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:59.660
"The Pursuer, who hunts down
the bearer of the sign,

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.160
will not rest until his target is slain.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:05.300
The Pursuer hunts down those branded by the curse,

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:09.060
as if each Undead soul that he claims
will atone one of his sins."

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:10.844
I love the concept of this boss.

00:16:10.844 --> 00:16:14.500
That feeling you get when you see
him fly towards you on that eagle,

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:17.960
and realizing I'm halfway through the level,
and I have to fight a boss now?!

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.920
then if you have the courage to fight him, you can get your ass kicked,

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:24.100
or you can jump off the ledge
and run away completely,

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.720
there are two options open to you.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:28.540
I decided to take him on,
and needless to say...

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:29.820
..I regretted it.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.220
I regretted it a lot.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.980
But my curiosity had to be satisfied,

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:37.820
so I came back on another character.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:40.520
I have 30 Soul Arrows,
and I know his moveset.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.640
So I'm gonna try,
and take him on.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.660
The one thing about this boss
that makes him easy:

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:47.753
is that he has
a very limited move set.

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:50.300
And he tells his moves
really obviously.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.660
That stab attack will curse you
if you get too close,

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:54.680
but like I said:
you can see it coming a mile away.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:57.360
And this is the attack right there,

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:58.880
that's the one you hit him after.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.840
He'll raise his shield
and dash at you:

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:02.880
roll out of the way,
It's your only option.

00:17:02.880 --> 00:17:04.620
And then counter attack, once.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.860
You might be able to get two hits in,
but one is safe.

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:10.260
I only had 30 Soul Arrows
and a dagger for this fight,

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.360
and luckily;

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:14.200
you just have enough Soul Arrows
to take him out.

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:16.140
Don't waste any
on the way here, use 30.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:18.460
With a Sorcerer,
you'll be able to take him out.

00:17:18.820 --> 00:17:22.360
For killing the Pursuer;
we get a Ring of Blades,
which increases physical damage.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.140
And we get his souls.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:26.980
If you don't kill him in here,
you have the chance of killing him later.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.840
But do you get anything extra
for killing him early?

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.360
No, unfortunately you don't.

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:34.350
Back on our main character,
we decide to go a different way.

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:36.018
This is the route
we traveled up earlier.

00:17:36.018 --> 00:17:38.052
And on the right you see
all the decrepit housing.

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:39.380
We're gonna make this jump.

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:40.940
I'm going to take out
some enemies here.

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:43.620
And we're eventually
going to make it to this cave.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.800
Once you get in:
just keep running straight through,
nothing's going to kill you(!)

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.600
Up this hill we'll meet Cale,

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:52.880
who's a great example of why talking to NPC's
will give you some great rewards.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.760
He's also one of those few characters
who's nice to you.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.940
Even though his mind has been decayed
by the curse.

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:01.920
CALE:
"Oh, I'm sorry.

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:03.660
I was just…

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.600
..daydreaming, I think.

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.220
My name is Cale.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:10.370
I am a traveller,
like yourself.

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:14.060
I'm navigating the continent
to create a map.

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:16.760
Have you seen Majula?

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.340
There's a rather spacious mansion there.

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:23.160
I…I've made it my temporary home.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:27.560
Inside the mansion,
I found a strange map.

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:29.520
Like none I'd ever seen.

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.800
I believe that it's
a map of Drangleic.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:38.440
Now I'm travelling the land to prove it.

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:43.380
Yes, yes, that's it!
That's why I came to the kingdom!

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:49.220
Wait…No, that wasn't it…

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:53.580
Then what? I don't seem to recall…"

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.200
In the next episode:

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.060
We travel to this crumbling city,
filled with these ancient giants.

00:18:59.060 --> 00:19:02.400
This one, the second one you fight,
gave me Sublime Bone Dust,

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:06.380
which you can burn in the Majula bonfire
to make your Estus Flask stronger.

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:08.380
I recommend going here early.

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.340
Another great item is available further on,

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:13.360
which stops you from losing so much health
once you're Hollowed.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.640
This is found just before
the Cathedral of Blue,

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:19.960
the drawbridge of which can be lowered,
if you take out the giants.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:24.260
And once we go up there,
we'll find an old friend waiting inside...

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:27.080
FOG GATE RUSTLES

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:31.000
Click the bonfire to figure out what
"kindling the channel" will do.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:35.260
This is a campaign I'm going to launch soon, 
and it's going to bring some amazing results.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:38.980
I actually can't wait to read
the comments about Dark Souls 2:

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:41.080
so if you have an experience
that you want to share,

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:43.600
or something you've found,
or something that you just want to talk about,

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:45.060
then please post below.

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:47.300
Preferably keep it about
what we discussed in this episode

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:49.300
to avoid spoilers for other people.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:52.842
But generally, I think,
you guys expect spoilers at this point.

00:19:52.842 --> 00:19:55.380
So yeah, let me know.
I'll catch you guys next time!

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:59.840
So there are some new mechanics in Dark Souls 2,
that I feel like you guys need to know about.

00:19:59.850 --> 00:20:02.700
These are things
that aren't explained in-game,

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.960
and whether you're new
to the Souls Series or not...

